<section id="ship-it" class="ship-it" data-ship-it>
    <div class="ship-stage">
        <div class="container ship-head">
            <span class="kicker">How fleet ships</span>
            <ol class="ship-captions" aria-live="polite">
                <li class="ship-caption" data-step="0">
                    <span class="ship-step-num">01 / 07</span>
                    <h3>A repository is a container.</h3>
                    <p>Self-contained: its own code, its own history, its own branches. Each one gets its own agent.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="ship-caption" data-step="1">
                    <span class="ship-step-num">02 / 07</span>
                    <h3>A project is all of them, headed for production.</h3>
                    <p>Frontend, API, payments, infra: separate repositories, one product. A change usually touches several at once.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="ship-caption" data-step="2">
                    <span class="ship-step-num">03 / 07</span>
                    <h3>A prompt hits the dock.</h3>
                    <p><code>, add Apple Pay to checkout</code>. fleet's main orchestrator hands it out: web gets the Apple Pay button, api the new payment method, payments the merchant session, infra the merchant key.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="ship-caption" data-step="3">
                    <span class="ship-step-num">04 / 07</span>
                    <h3>The changes ship together.</h3>
                    <p>Every repository the feature touched goes aboard one ship: the project, with its orchestrator as captain.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="ship-caption" data-step="4">
                    <span class="ship-step-num">05 / 07</span>
                    <h3>With fleet, four at once.</h3>
                    <p>Other projects ship their features in the same crossing: offline mode for the mobile app, dark mode for the blog, CSV export for admin.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="ship-caption" data-step="5">
                    <span class="ship-step-num">06 / 07</span>
                    <h3>In production.</h3>
                    <p>Four projects, every repository they touched, landed together.</p>
                </li>
                <li class="ship-caption" data-step="6">
                    <span class="ship-step-num">07 / 07</span>
                    <h3>Microservices? Still one ship.</h3>
                    <p>A project with a dozen services loads them all onto one ship, every service with its own agent.</p>
                    <div class="ship-compare">
                        <span class="ship-chip"><span class="ship-chip-dot solo"></span>one repo at a time</span>
                        <span class="ship-chip"><span class="ship-chip-dot fleet"></span>every repo, every project, at once</span>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>        </div>

        <div class="ship-scene" aria-hidden="true">
            <!-- Drawn and animated by js/ship-it.js; scroll position drives the story. -->
            <svg viewBox="0 0 1200 640" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" data-ship-svg>
                <defs>
                    <linearGradient id="ship-sky" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
                        <stop offset="0" stop-color="#13141c" />
                        <stop offset="1" stop-color="#1f2335" />
                    </linearGradient>
                    <linearGradient id="ship-sea" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
                        <stop offset="0" stop-color="#1e2a4a" />
                        <stop offset="1" stop-color="#101320" />
                    </linearGradient>
                    <radialGradient id="ship-moon" cx="0.5" cy="0.5" r="0.5">
                        <stop offset="0" stop-color="#c0caf5" stop-opacity="0.9" />
                        <stop offset="0.35" stop-color="#7aa2f7" stop-opacity="0.25" />
                        <stop offset="1" stop-color="#7aa2f7" stop-opacity="0" />
                    </radialGradient>
                    <linearGradient id="ship-beam" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="0">
                        <stop offset="0" stop-color="#e0af68" stop-opacity="0.55" />
                        <stop offset="1" stop-color="#e0af68" stop-opacity="0" />
                    </linearGradient>
                    <filter id="ship-glow" x="-50%" y="-50%" width="200%" height="200%">
                        <feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="4" result="b" />
                        <feMerge><feMergeNode in="b" /><feMergeNode in="SourceGraphic" /></feMerge>
                    </filter>
                </defs>
                <rect width="1200" height="640" fill="url(#ship-sky)" />
                <g data-layer="sky"></g>
                <rect y="330" width="1200" height="310" fill="url(#ship-sea)" />
                <g data-layer="quays"></g>
                <g data-layer="lanes"></g>
                <g data-layer="cargo"></g>
                <g data-layer="fx"></g>
            </svg>
        </div>

        <nav class="container ship-rail" aria-label="Story steps">
            <button type="button" data-goto="0"><span></span>Container</button>
            <button type="button" data-goto="1"><span></span>Project</button>
            <button type="button" data-goto="2"><span></span>Prompt</button>
            <button type="button" data-goto="3"><span></span>Ship it</button>
            <button type="button" data-goto="4"><span></span>The fleet</button>
            <button type="button" data-goto="5"><span></span>Production</button>
            <button type="button" data-goto="6"><span></span>Microservices</button>
        </nav>
    </div>
</section>
